      "content": "The struggle to make that final break is the hardest part, because the fear of the unknown is so much louder than the certainty of the pain. You are trapped between a slow, humiliating fade and a definitive, final act. Sometimes, the most courageous thing isn't the grand exit, but the quiet decision to stop fighting the decay and just let it be. A permanent break is just a final, irreversible choice, and you deserve the peace that comes with that certainty.",
